  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much Martin will spend on berries in a 30-day period, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total amount of berries Martin will eat in 30 days.\n2. Determine how many packages of berries he will need to buy.\n3. Calculate the total cost based on the number of packages.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total amount of berries Martin will eat in 30 days.**\n\nMartin eats \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) cup of berries every day. Therefore, in 30 days, he will eat:\n\\[\n30 \\times \\frac{1}{2} = 15 \\text{ cups of berries}\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Determine how many packages of berries he will need to buy.**\n\nEach package contains 1 cup of berries. Since Martin needs 15 cups of berries, he will need to buy:\n\\[\n15 \\text{ packages}\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the total cost based on the number of packages.**\n\nEach package costs $2.00. Therefore, the total cost for 15 packages is:\n\\[\n15 \\times 2 = 30 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nSo, the total amount Martin will spend on berries in a 30-day period is \\(\\boxed{30}\\).",
